= Raised-energy CFF review: complete file coverage
<raised-energy-cff-review-complete-file-coverage>
#quote(block: true)[
Historical record for the revisions and dates stated below. Its test counts, API descriptions and continuation instructions do not certify or govern the reconstructed stack. See the #link("raised-energy-cff-stack-review.typ")[stack review] and #link("raised-energy-cff-stack-review-validation.typ")[fresh validation record];, together with #link("architecture-current.typ")[current architecture] and #link("../../CONTRIBUTING.typ")[CONTRIBUTING.typ];. The original body is preserved.
]

Review completed 2026-09-08. Base `395610143576507503fd2c785db3ba62340f4277`; target `91142139e1fde44cc4709a35ad090631d27ca451`. Git three-dot diff: #strong[392 files];, 76,394 added and 7,976 deleted lines.

Coverage: #strong[186 full changed-hunk reviews];, #strong[205 generated-artifact audits];, #strong[1 binary inventory];. No code diff remains unreviewed. All added/removed code hunks were read; new code files were read in full. Selected surrounding callers and invariants were traced. Reading source does not mean every executable path was tested.

`full_hunks` includes complete changed-hunk inspection of code, tests, configuration and prose; new files were read in full. `artifact_audit` means the generated diff/body was read and format, source references and applicable consistency were checked, without independent numerical or semantic regeneration. `binary_inventory` records size/hash only. Lock files have full diff/manifest consistency review, not an audit of every dependency's upstream source.

Large-file split: the root reviewer read CFF module production lines 1--877 and the removed predecessor; the core-large reviewer read all test lines 878--6956. The complete shared generation (11,563 lines), shared evaluation (3,767 lines), and graph source mapper (7,013 lines) were read. All initially truncated source views were reread in smaller chunks.

All 200 snapshot bodies/envelopes and source references were inspected; 198 scalar snapshots have no active test consumer. All 15 changed DOTs passed Graphviz parsing. JSON/TOML parsing and local JSON schema references were checked. Nix workspace graph nodes/edges were checked against manifests; schemas and Guppy output were not regenerated. Historical acceptance/scalar snapshot values were not independently rederived. The scalar-model JSON's only semantic changes are three `goldstone: false` values.

`crates/gammalooprs/state_map.bin`: 22,753 bytes; SHA-256 `dca35a6485e22e528fc15b627ae2af496fa7f7a410a81e9fa21f7b1f2ac521be`. The hash agrees with the documented historical export. No binary semantic decoding or certification is claimed.

Reviewer labels identify parallel review slices, not extra independent reviews of every row. Root-owned CFF code plus core-large-owned tests form a complete review of that file. The report and evidence appendices are new review artifacts and are outside the branch diff counted here.

